    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d993">

                <pb facs="0963" n="705" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg705"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.731/318</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6 p. m.</hi>] </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1582. At my request, the censor counted the whole number of telegrams going both
                    was for three days and reports that the number stopped between the United States
                    and Holland was 14 per cent of the total number and between Scandinavian
                    countries and the United States, 3 per cent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
